      "matn_ar": "قال: قال رسول الله صلى الله عليه وآله: ان قاتل الحسين في تابوت من النار عليه نصف عذاب اهل النار وقد تشد يداه ورجلاه بسلاسل من نار فينكس في النار حتى يقع في قعر جهنم وله ريح يتعوذ اهل النار إلى ربهم من شدة نتنه وهو فيها خالد ذائق العذاب الاليم كلما نضجت جلودهم بدل الله الجلود ليذوقوا العذاب الاليم، لا يفتر عنهم ساعة ويسقون من حميم جهنم، فالويل لهم من عذاب الله عزوجل.",
      "chain_type": "Alid (Rida)",
      "school": "Medina",
      "text_en": "And on his chain, he said: My father narrated to me, Ali ibn Al-Husayn, peace be upon them both, that he named Husn on his seventh day and derived it from the name of Al-Hasan. Al-Husayn mentioned that there was nothing between them except pregnancy. And on his chain, he said: My father narrated to me, Ali ibn Al-Husayn, peace be upon them both, that when Ali ibn Al-Husayn entered the resting place, he found a piece of bread lying down. He pushed it to a boy of his and said, 'O boy, remind me about this piece of bread when you leave and eat it.' When Al-Husayn, peace be upon him, left, he said, 'O boy, where is the piece of bread?' He said, 'I ate it, my master.' So Al-Husayn, peace be upon him, said, 'You are free by the will of Allah Almighty.' A man told him, 'I freed you, my lord.' He said, 'Yes. I heard my grandfather, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him and his progeny, saying: \"Whoever finds a piece of bread lying down, he wipes from it what he can wipe, washes what he can wash, and then eats it; it will not settle in his stomach until Allah frees him from the Fire. And I would not enslave a man whom Allah freed from the Fire.",
      "translation_confidence": 4,
      "translation_model": "google/gemma-4-e4b"
    },
    {
      "id": "rida_0021",
